  "Question": "Granny Smith has \\(\\$63.\\) Elberta has \\(\\$2\\) more than Anjou and Anjou has one-third as much as Granny Smith. How many dollars does Elberta have?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(17\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(19\\)",
    "D": "\\(21\\)",
    "E": "\\(23\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Find Anjou's amount first because Elberta has \\(2\\) dollars more than Anjou. One-third of \\(63\\) dollars means dividing it into \\(3\\) equal shares, so Anjou has \\(63\\div3=21\\) dollars. Therefore Elberta has\n\\[\n63\\div3+2=21+2=23\n\\]\ndollars, choice E.",
